      "side": 1,
      "message": "If a plugin registers an `EndpointType.REPLACE` module before `awaitPluginsLoaded()` resolves, `GrPluginEndpoints.registerModule` now invokes the `onNewEndpoint` callback immediately (and this microtask also initializes already-registered `REPLACE` modules). However, any `EndpointType.DECORATE` module registered on the same endpoint (or registered later before `awaitPluginsLoaded()`) will still run in the `awaitPluginsLoaded().then(...)` loop below and append its decoration element into the replaced endpoint. Should `initModule` skip `DECORATE` modules once a `REPLACE` module has already been initialized on this decorator?",
