      "writtenOn": "2026-10-26T18:23:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If a CDN asset URL is configured (`window.ASSETS_PATH`) and the primary script fails to load, `loadJsPlugin` falls back to `createScriptTag(urlWithoutAP)` via a custom `onerror` handler. Because `createScriptTag` only sets the default `this.failToLoad(...)` handler when `onerror` is omitted, a failure on the fallback script will not call `failToLoad`. For `gerrit-theme.js`, that means the plugin stays in `PluginState.PENDING` for the full 10-second `PLUGIN_LOADING_TIMEOUT_MS`, leaving `\u003cgr-main-header\u003e` hidden for 10 seconds before timing out. Consider passing an `onerror` handler to the fallback `createScriptTag(urlWithoutAP)` call (or letting `createScriptTag` always default to `failToLoad` when `onerror` is undefined).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 356,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 365,
        "endChar": 9999
      },
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "4db6c0d69d9d3bd75c7f13e282f73cd370bd5450",
